    "findings": [
      "The kernel recorded 3 undervoltage episode(s) totaling at least 36.0 seconds in this range.",
      "1 undervoltage episode(s) occurred within 15 seconds of logged USB activity; hub inrush, back-powering, a downstream device, or total USB load is a plausible trigger.",
      "The kernel also reported 1 USB over-current change event(s), which is direct evidence of a USB power-path disturbance.",
      "2 episode(s) had no nearby logged USB activity. The evidence therefore does not isolate the powered hub; the Pi supply, cable, connector, and upstream 5 V path remain suspects.",
      "There are also 1 storage I/O error event(s); verify filesystem and device health before trusting affected disks."
    ],
    "headline": "Pi input undervoltage is confirmed",
    "level": "critical",
    "next_steps": [
      "After safely unmounting affected storage, reboot with the powered hub disconnected to clear the sticky firmware history and establish a baseline.",
      "Repeat with a known-good short Pi power cable/supply, then add the powered hub with no downstream devices and add devices one at a time.",
      "Treat USB errors without undervoltage as data-path/device evidence; treat undervoltage without USB activity as Pi input-power-path evidence."
    ]
  },
